1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Ushiwaka, he's so awesome. Now I'm super pumped up. Let's go!

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Oh, I see, Lefty.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Oh, I see.

4
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,480
me

5
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:28,480
yeah

6
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:38,240
How you figure it out

7
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,200
Oh

8
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,200
Ah

9
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:03,980
How did Noya not get that?

10
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:06,040
Shake it off, get the next one.

11
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:06,880
Yeah.

12
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,120
No biggie.

13
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,820
Don't worry.

14
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,580
Give us a good one, Tai Chi.

15
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,200
That's going out.

16
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:18,880
Yes.

17
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,100
Sorry, guys.

18
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,520
Come on, let's go.

19
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:27,300
Come on, Tai Chi, get us another one.

20
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:30,260
I got it.

21
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,380
Sorry, man.

22
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,120
That's on me.

23
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,640
Everyone is so nervous.

24
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,740
We're making beginner's mistakes.

25
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:41,180
Damn.

26
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:44,140
We need to focus for this is going to be a slaughter.

27
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,480
Don't panic, guys.

28
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:49,220
Are you guys getting distracted by all the cameras?

29
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,600
Just ignore them.

30
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:51,600
Listen up.

31
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,620
Get your heads out of your big dumb asses.

32
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:56,560
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

33
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,980
We all need to chill out.

34
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:58,780
You included.

35
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:00,740
Sorry about him.

36
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:06,060
He's using the old trick of meltdown and freak out to help ease the team's nerves, I guess.

37
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,100
I don't really care how they do it.

38
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,700
As long as they can relax and score some points.

39
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:11,760
Crap.

40
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,320
The ref is going to have it out for me now.

41
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,540
All right, make it count.

42
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:20,980
Got it.

43
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,780
All right, that went up nicely.

44
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:24,800
Yeah.

45
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,440
Nice receive.

46
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,600
Pushy walk up.

47
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:30,620
Pushy walk up.

48
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:38,440
You got it.

49
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,240
Keep at it.

50
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,000
Pushy walk up.

51
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:42,820
Pushy walk up.

52
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:43,480
I'm adjusting.

53
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:44,660
Pushy walk up.

54
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:47,820
I promise.

55
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,420
Third time's the charm.

56
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,000
Oh, man.

57
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,380
I thought there was something different about that guy.

58
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,660
Is the guy in the number one jersey left-handed?

59
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:02,980
I noticed my big brother always comes in from the left, so that must be why this guy comes

60
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:03,740
in from the right.

61
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:04,880
That's right.

62
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:08,900
And it's pretty rare, too, so it feels like he was born to be the ace.

63
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:09,560
Huh?

64
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:15,040
The position Ushi Waka plays is called the opposite, located diagonally from the opposing

65
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:18,520
team's center, so Karashino's opposite would be where Daichi is now.

66
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:23,660
Depending on how the opposite moves, it can change the synergy of how a team normally plays.

67
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:26,800
One way to counter that is to put someone like Daichi there.

68
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,800
He's a flexible, all-around player with solid defense.

69
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,160
It's a pretty common tactic in high school games.

70
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,040
Another approach is to put your heavy hitters there, like Ushi Waka.

71
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:40,620
Opposites don't serve or receive, even if they're in the front or the back row.

72
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:43,560
Their only real objective is to be ready to attack.

73
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:46,800
We used to call them super aces.

74
00:04:55,800 --> 00:05:00,780
Dude, I mean, I get that the bastard is all big and tall and has a lot of power and everything,

75
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:04,040
but does being a lefty really give him such an advantage?

76
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,560
Suppertime!

77
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:13,080
Nice kick, Tanaka!

78
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,240
Good, we finally scored a point!

79
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,780
Yeah, that-a-boy, bro!

80
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,480
So tell me, what's so special about being left-handed?

81
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,260
Mmm, okay.

82
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:33,280
Okay, so because players normally face mostly right-handed opponents, left-handers turn out

83
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,020
to be more tricky than you would expect.

84
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:41,700
So for example, when a solo blocker makes a jump, they align with the opponent's dominant arm,

85
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:45,560
which ultimately puts them in a position that's about one shoulder-width away.

86
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,900
Under most circumstances, it results in a predetermined outcome.

87
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:54,920
But if the player jumps purely on their intuition...

88
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,140
A delayed spike!

89
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,660
...they won't be able to block it in time.

90
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,880
What is Karasuro doing?

91
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,440
Have these nincompoos forgotten how to block?

92
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,700
Their dilemma is adapting to a left-handed player,

93
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:11,500
who's also equipped with top-tier firepower.

94
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:15,160
That's what makes Ushiwaka a force to be reckoned with.

95
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:19,140
So Ushiwaka's already earned them four points since we started?

96
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,160
Yeah.

97
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,280
He seems pretty reliable, and they recognize that.

98
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:27,320
Their goal was most likely to set him up so they could claim an early lead.

99
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:33,920
Huh? What's that sound?

100
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:37,120
Oh, that buzzer means it's a technical timeout.

101
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:38,160
And what's that?

102
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:42,440
It's a mandatory timeout taken when one of the teams reaches 8 or 16 points.

103
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,920
They mostly only use it in five-set matches.

104
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,320
At least, I think.

105
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,660
This is important, guys.

106
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,440
Listen up.

107
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:51,420
Blocking is all about finding that sweet spot and the timing.

108
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:53,900
Even if you realize you can't stop their attacks,

109
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:56,580
just remember, it's crucial to be in the way.

110
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:58,860
If all else fails, just make contact.

111
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,880
Let them know you're there.

112
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:00,800
Yes, sir!

113
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:12,580
One touch!

114
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,320
Shit!

115
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:17,700
Man!

116
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:19,720
Ushiwaka is relentless!

117
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,880
It's okay!

118
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:21,780
We'll recover!

119
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:23,180
That's good!

120
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,240
Just keep it up!

121
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,140
Keep reminding him that wall is there.

122
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,020
We'll get our openings soon.

123
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,840
Shira Torizawa has Ushiwaka.

124
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:33,620
Huh?

125
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:37,300
Then, Karasuno has me, the comeback kid.

126
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,160
Oh!

127
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,160
Yeah, that's true.

128
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:44,060
Stopping all of Ushiwaka's attacks won't happen.

129
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:47,120
And it'll be even less likely we'll be able to get the ball from him.

130
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:52,140
However, we'll have a shot if we make his impossible spikes playable.

131
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:53,500
Hmm?

132
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:56,080
It's called total defense.

133
00:07:57,240 --> 00:08:01,260
Studying his past games, Ushiwaka likes to utilize the cross block.

134
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:03,240
So we'll find our opening that way.

135
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:07,040
We'll counter by having Nishinoya here, where the straight path will be.

136
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:09,920
We'll force him to hit to our libero.

137
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,700
Good timing, guys.

138
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:27,500
Nishinoya here, Ushiwaka!

139
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:29,460
Ushiwaka!

140
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:31,460
Ushiwaka!

141
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,920
Nishinoya never has this much trouble.

142
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,320
This is serious!

143
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:40,460
I think that's due to the ball's rotation.

144
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:47,640
When a left-handed player hits the ball, the spin is slightly different than when a right-handed player hits it.

145
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,160
Obviously, you aren't allowed to hold the ball in volleyball.

146
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,900
So the time frame to affect the ball is a very small window.

147
00:08:55,800 --> 00:09:00,960
So in that moment, if your receive is even slightly off, the ball will go off course.

148
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,040
It's a chance ball!

149
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,360
Damn it! I'm so sorry!

150
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:16,880
Timing is off.

151
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,040
Total defense, huh?

152
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,840
Even getting the timing right on these blocks is far from easy.

153
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:35,560
Concentrate, guys!

154
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:39,320
How confident are you about stopping Ushiwaka's spikes?

155
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:45,600
You know there's no way I'll be able to beat Ushiwaka.

156
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:54,100
I'm spending too much of my attention on Ushiwaka.

157
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:58,060
Is Goggles even trying down there?

158
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:01,100
Where the hell's your fighting spirit, kid?

159
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,000
You fall asleep?

160
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:05,400
They're starting to link their attacks together pretty well now.

161
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:08,440
We have to hurry up and get that big jerk under control!

162
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,660
I sure hope they can learn to go against their muscle memory.

163
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,780
They're used to blocking right-hand shots.

164
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:19,100
My bad!

165
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,400
Don't worry!

166
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:25,000
Yeah, well, at least my brother is the type of player who remains calm in high-pressure situations.

167
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,280
Asi, you got this!

168
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:29,240
He doesn't believe in his own strengths.

169
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:32,080
Or trust his instincts, either.

170
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,120
Nice receive!

171
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,400
Shouldn't you help build his confidence?

172
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:38,720
I meant it as praise!

173
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,720
You see, with my brother, he doesn't ever lose his composure.

174
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:47,860
The only information he knows he can trust is what is directly in his line of sight.

175
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:49,260
Okay.

176
00:10:49,260 --> 00:11:08,600
I saw that my brother adjusted to the left to put himself in the spike's path.

177
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:10,220
What happened there?

178
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,960
You're getting really close.

179
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,320
You're actually able to react to what he's sending over.

180
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:20,240
I have a feeling these are not his full power spikes.

181
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:23,620
He's probably still just warming up his engine.

182
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:28,340
He also seems to be focusing on finding ways to get his spikes through all of our blocking.

183
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,100
Back at middle school?

184
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:32,540
We used to have a lefty on the team.

185
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:34,380
Man, it was hard to set that guy up.

186
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:39,320
So, with Ushiwaka's attacks, even a love tap could turn out to be a deadly weapon.

187
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:41,780
Suki!

188
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,480
Did you get a stinger on your finger?

189
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:44,880
Uh, yeah.

190
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,160
How unfortunate that you worded it that way.

191
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:47,860
Here.

192
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:48,860
Let me help.

193
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:49,820
Thank you.

194
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:53,120
This is a pretty common injury, isn't it?

195
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,780
I feel pretty lucky that I barely even nicked it.

196
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:58,240
That should do it.

197
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:58,820
Thanks.

198
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,320
Did I even flinch?

199
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:03,840
No.

200
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:07,000
I realized after I jumped that I was going to fail.

201
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:09,520
It's pretty obvious now that I think about it.

202
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:19,440
You guys are looking mighty stiff!

203
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:21,320
Let's all just relax, okay?

204
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:21,820
Uh-huh.

205
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:22,960
Huh?

206
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:30,820
Our research showed that Ushiwaka's serves are solid, right?

207
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:35,320
While he doesn't have the same monstrous attack or precision as Oikawa,

208
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,180
there's still a lot of power behind his shots.

209
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:51,460
No sense!

210
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:52,080
Yeah, nice!

211
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:55,380
I just don't get it.

212
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,640
He's in high school?

213
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,120
This is getting hard to watch.

214
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:02,480
I hope our guys don't let it bring him down.

215
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,260
Sorry, send me another!

216
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:05,080
Roger that!

217
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:08,880
I'm glad I'm not in the position to receive one of his serves.

218
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,560
There's no way I could take that head-on.

219
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,260
Shira Torzawa totally shut us down this set.

220
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:20,620
We should take this one as a lost cause and save our energy for the next.

221
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:22,960
Come on.

222
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:24,460
Come on.

223
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:25,980
Come on.

224
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:27,900
Come on.

225
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,620
Keep it going!

226
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:29,240
Come on.

227
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:30,300
Come on.

228
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:31,580
Come on!

229
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,500
Come on!

230
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,360
Do it!

231
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:51,700
It's up!

232
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:52,200
Let's go!

233
00:13:52,200 --> 00:14:22,180
We'll be right back.

234
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:30,540
Nice ball, Kageyama!

235
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,500
Kageyama even faked me out with that play.

236
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:36,300
Well, he made us a promise and he came through again.

237
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:37,960
I'm so proud of him.

238
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,760
Can't believe he motioned for the spike, but then made us set.

239
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,880
That guy's truly a disciple of Oikawa.

240
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:47,700
Huh? Oh, is that so?

241
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,180
How disgusting.

242
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:51,880
Look at you, Mr. Cool as a Cucumber!

243
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:52,620
What you thinking?

244
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:56,720
Yeah, well, no one rattles me more than that asshole Oikawa.

245
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,560
So that's how your brain works.

246
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:00,720
All right!

247
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,000
My turn to fight!

248
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:06,540
Look!

249
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:07,600
He does his in!

250
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:08,840
He must be thrilled.

251
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,120
I wonder if they're going to keep rotating him to the back like last time.

252
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:13,560
Get him some points!

253
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,060
Okay, let's do this!

254
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,380
There really isn't much to you.

255
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:20,200
I guess that's why they stick you in as the middle blocker.

256
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:30,020
He really doesn't go for any of the serves.

257
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:32,740
Looks like he's getting ready for a back row attack.

258
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:39,020
A one-man decode attack.

259
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,580
Do you like that?

260
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:49,160
Give us a good one!

261
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,320
He's out!

262
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,360
Excellent call!

263
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:59,700
Keep taking advantage of Shiratoi Zawa's mistakes!

264
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:01,200
We'll be able to break through!

265
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:07,700
Great job!

266
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,080
Yeah!

267
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:12,120
Good old reliable Kageyama and Nishinoya.

268
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,040
They always give us everything they've got.

269
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:14,780
Yeah.

270
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:33,120
I hope Ushiwaka noticed my super straight shot!

271
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:34,780
Nice receive, man.

272
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,620
Thanks, but I couldn't return it.

273
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,040
We really should look for validation elsewhere.

274
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:41,520
Let's do it, Kageyama.

275
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:42,580
Yeah.

276
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:50,900
Ushiwaka!

277
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:56,020
Hell yeah!

278
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:56,960
He got it!

279
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:59,360
Damn, these are so hard to get.

280
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,080
Hinata!

281
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:02,320
Get last hit!

282
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:06,720
The ball ricocheted!

283
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:08,280
They should be able to get to that.

284
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:10,080
One more time, guys!

285
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:10,160
One more time, guys!

286
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:20,500
I'm Shouyo Hinata from the Karasuno parking lot.

287
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:24,900
And I'm going to Nationals after I kick your ass.

288
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:34,260
Oh, come on!

289
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,960
He doesn't do that!

290
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:37,980
Over to me.

291
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:55,920
HushouWaka!

292
00:17:55,920 --> 00:18:03,900
Well, now, is Mr. Sirius over there getting his little undies all twisted up?

293
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,760
Color me intrigued!

294
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:10,000
Don't worry, we're just getting started!

295
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,100
Take this out!

296
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,600
Suck it up, boys!

297
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,240
Hey, Ishiwaka, are you in Karasuno's number 10 buds?

298
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:19,000
I met him on the street.

299
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:19,760
The street?

300
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:23,180
He told me he was going to beat me and go to nationals.

301
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:24,340
I'll see!

302
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:25,480
Yeah.

303
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:26,520
It is.

304
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:32,240
Come to think of it, didn't you get scolded for letting some strange kid into the school?

305
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:33,720
Oh, okay!

306
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:35,940
He's a mouthy kid who picks fights?

307
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,280
I get why you like him so much!

308
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,540
Actually, I hate him.

309
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:42,780
I loathe arrogance with nothing to back it up.

310
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,200
Huh?

311
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:46,580
Did my ears deceive me?

312
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:52,200
If Shorty can make the great stoic Ushiwaka have an emotional response like that...

313
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:56,900
It sounds like this could be a lot of fun for me as well.

314
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:59,680
There's nothing to worry about.

315
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:03,120
You might as well consider that first set your warm-up match.

316
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:07,540
Ushiwaka scored 11 points, which was nearly half of their overall total.

317
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:10,000
But the fact that he's getting the ball so often...

318
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Proves that you guys are getting under Shira Torizawa's skin.

319
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,360
They are using him as a crutch.

320
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,340
And he may not seem like it.

321
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:23,120
But Ushiwaka's a normal human, with normal human limits to his stamina.

322
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:26,380
So keep wearing him down by using those indirect attacks.

323
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,120
Now get out there and kick some asses!

324
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:29,580
Right!

325
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,620
You guys are going down!

326
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:36,920
Let's start off strong, Goshki!

327
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:37,880
Right!

328
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,560
There it is.

329
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:45,480
Oh!

330
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,000
Okay.

331
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:51,260
Synchronized attack!

332
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:52,200
Wait.

333
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:53,940
Are all four of them going to attack?

334
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,160
You're right!

335
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,660
Go, go, Russell, go!

336
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:04,680
Push it, push it!

337
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,300
Well, that was kind of misleading.

338
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,900
This will be interesting.

339
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,500
Serve it where the sun don't shine!

340
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,000
I got it!

341
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:15,740
Nice receive!

342
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,180
Nice!

343
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:19,820
Yeah!

344
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,200
They're getting what they want.

345
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:27,440
They're executing plays without using Ushiwaka, which means that they're feeling pretty comfortable right now.

346
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:34,620
If their center line joins in and starts attacking us, then of course we'll have too much to deal with and it'll mean big trouble.

347
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:40,340
Our focus is the same.

348
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,820
All eyes should be on Shira Torizawa's captain Ushiwaka.

349
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:48,160
So most importantly, we need to create a strategy to nullify his attack.

350
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,620
Otherwise, we don't stand a chance.

351
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:53,880
We need to keep wearing him down, one attack after another.

352
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:56,160
Everything depends on it.

353
00:20:56,160 --> 00:21:01,700
All right, he's patched it.

354
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:03,220
Ushiwaka!

355
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,100
Nice to meet you!

356
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,480
Shake it off, Noya.

357
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:13,540
Even if they steal warrants, we need to stick to our guns, right, coach?

358
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:14,580
Right.

359
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:15,540
Ushiwaka!

360
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:18,660
It's already that punch serve again!

361
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,620
Do it, Ushiwaka!

362
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:33,260
Just as planned!

363
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,840
Those tears planned, too?

364
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,460
Awesome, Tanaka!

365
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,120
Okay, we're staying with them, Miss Zip!

366
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:43,160
Karasuno will have this in the bag if they can get accustomed to Ushiwaka's left-handed shots.

367
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:46,800
She'll be begging for mercy when I'm done with you, Ushiwaka!

368
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:49,640
Did something happen between Hinata and Ushiwaka?

369
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,500
Apparently, the two of them butted heads over something.

370
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:53,180
Huh?

371
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:56,400
He's gonna give our school a bad name doing stupid crap like that.

372
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:01,000
Don't play it safe.

373
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:02,460
Don't be cowards.

374
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,180
And don't hold back.

375
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,640
This is our only way through this.

376
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:07,360
Ah!

377
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:09,280
Chance ball!

378
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:12,540
Pass it to me!

379
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,200
It's his diagonal jump again.

380
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:40,160
You're gonna have to come through me first if you want to take down Ushiwaka, shall we?

381
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,620
See you later.

